# Extraction stub — nougat.mmd

**Status:** placeholder. Full Nougat OCR/text extraction of the source PDF
was not run for this replication; the replication was performed from a manual
reading of the PDF with numerical extraction of text-quoted quantities plus
manual figure digitization.

## Paper identity
- **DOI:** 10.2147/JHC.S383959
- **Source PDF (SHA-cited filename):** 2c94a15708907c2998f2f6db1ac1b1e9186b39cd.pdf
- **License:** CC BY-NC 3.0 (Dove Medical Press)
- **Title (short):** BNCT in radioresistant hepatocellular carcinoma (Huang et al., 2022)
- **Journal:** Journal of Hepatocellular Carcinoma

## Text-quoted quantities extracted for replication
See `report/artifacts_summary.md` for the extracted quantities that fed the
LQ refits and RBE recomputation. These were taken by direct reading of the
PDF text (Tables 1, 4; Fig 1C text-quoted mean survival fractions at 1, 2,
5 Gy per curve) and manual figure digitization (Fig 3B BNCT clonogenic).

## What is NOT in this stub
- Full body-text nougat markdown.
- Machine-readable table rows for Table 5.
- Equation extractions.
- Reference-list extraction.

## How to regenerate a real nougat.mmd
```
# From workspace root, with nougat installed:
nougat --markdown \
  ~/Dropbox/REPLICATE-PROJECT/lucid-pdf-corpus/2c94a15708907c2998f2f6db1ac1b1e9186b39cd.pdf \
  --out ~/Dropbox/REPLICATE-PROJECT/LUCID-replications/lucid-bnct-radioresistant-hcc/extraction/
```

Nougat model recommended: `0.1.0-small` for speed, `0.1.0-base` for accuracy.
The replication's numerical results do not depend on this file being
generated.
